#!/usr/bin/env sh
# pre-push — the local gate before code leaves this machine.
#
# WHAT CI ACTUALLY DOES, because the comment that stood here got it wrong. It
# said GitHub Actions does NOT run on push or PR, that both workflows were
# workflow_dispatch-only "because this repo does not pay for Actions", and that
# "a PR showing an empty status-check rollup is the designed state, not a
# pending one". That stopped being true when the billing block cleared before
# 2026-07-05 and the `on:` keys were restored — see the HISTORY OF THE `on:` KEY
# section at the top of .github/workflows/tests.yml. MEASURED on PR #300,
# 2026-08-14: two checks started by themselves and both concluded SUCCESS —
# demos (45s) and verify-core (3m45s). An empty rollup on a PR is now a sign
# that something is broken, not the design.
#
# Both workflows trigger on `pull_request`, and on `push` to main only:
#
#   - a pull request gets tests.yml (`make verify-core`) and demos.yml
#   - a push to a branch with no PR open gets NOTHING
#
# The second line is why this hook still earns its several minutes, and why it
# is not redundant with tests.yml even though both call `make verify-core`: the
# hook covers the window before a PR exists. It is also not a superset of CI.
# demos.yml builds and runs the demo targets plus an AddressSanitizer step, and
# MEASURED against the Makefile, none of those are in verify-core (see the
# comment at the top of demos.yml).
#
# Do not read this comment as a statement about CI coverage in a later session.
# Read `gh pr view <n> --json statusCheckRollup` and look at each `conclusion`.
# A comment is not an instrument.
#
# `make verify-core`, NOT `make verify`. verify-core is the full probe net minus
# the CompCert bootstrap pilot, and CLAUDE.md designates it "the authoritative
# ccomp-free gate; safe for pre-push on any machine". `make verify` additionally
# needs an opam CompCert switch, and installing ccomp is still an open item
# (V1-ccomp-install, docs/COMPCERT_AUDIT.md) — so on a machine without it this
# hook failed EVERY push at ccomp-build. A gate that cannot pass locally gets
# bypassed habitually, and a habitually-bypassed gate is no gate at all.
#
# Run `make verify` by hand when you have the CompCert switch and want the
# bootstrap pilot on top of this.
#
# Emergency bypass (use sparingly): git push --no-verify
set -e

echo "[pre-push] make verify-core"
make verify-core
echo "[pre-push] make test"
make test
